{"name":"Maximum Red","hex":"#d92121","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maximum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The highest limit.","The greatest value of a set or other mathematical structure, especially the global maximum or a local maximum of a function."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["To the highest degree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maximum"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maximum and minimum","blocks":[{"text":"In mathematical analysis, the maximum and minimum of a function are, respectively, the greatest and least value taken by the function. Known generically as extrema, they may be defined either within a given range or on the entire domain of a function. Pierre de Fermat was one of the first mathematicians to propose a general technique, adequality, for finding the maxima and minima of functions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Extrema_example_original.svg/330px-Extrema_example_original.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximum_and_minimum","wikidata":"Q845060"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg/500px-Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg/500px-Modell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peano surface, a counterexample to some criteria of local maxima of the 19th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AModell_einer_Peanoschen_Fl%C3%A4che_-Schilling_XLIX%2C_1-.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/MaximumParaboloid.png/500px-MaximumParaboloid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/MaximumParaboloid.png/500px-MaximumParaboloid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The global maximum is the point at the top","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaximumParaboloid.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/MaximumCounterexample.png/500px-MaximumCounterexample.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm